Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 00:27:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: World Cup support with neutral-venue model and
 automatic data refresh
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

World Cup (football-data.org code WC, stable id 1)
- Added to FD_LEAGUES so it flows through fixtures, refresh and analysis
  exactly like a league — the 2026 edition (kicking off June 11) is covered
  by the provider's free tier.
- New TOURNAMENT_LEAGUES handling: venues are neutral, so team strength is
  one combined scored/conceded average mirrored into both home/away splits
  instead of a meaningless home/away separation.
- Pre-kickoff fallback: while the current edition has no finished matches,
  histories come from the previous edition; debutant teams with no history
  at all get the field-wide average (flagged with played=0) so their lambda
  doesn't collapse to zero. As group-stage results land, every 6h refresh
  folds them in automatically.
- Frontend: Copa do Mundo 🏆 added to the fixtures league filter; the
  analyse flow picks it up automatically from /leagues.

Automation
- Scheduler now ingests every 6 hours (00/06/12/18 UTC) instead of once a
  day — important while the World Cup has multiple matchdays per day.
- Fresh deploys bootstrap themselves: if the database has no leagues at
  startup, an immediate ingestion job is queued, so nobody has to click
  'Atualizar' on a new environment.

Tests: 3 new (tournament registration, neutral averages, prev-edition
fallback + debutant handling) — 44/44 passing.
